        "id": 19984,
        "name": "drkrash1969",
        "username": "drkrash1969",
        "avatar_template": "/letter_avatar_proxy/v4/letter/d/eada6e/{size}.png",
        "created_at": "2020-06-14T15:39:09.000Z",
        "cooked": "<p>In your games, do you allow flying combatants to be safe from grounded opponents (excepting, of course, attacks expliciting defined as ranged attacks like blasts or thrown cars)?</p>\n<p>To put it another way, can your close combat fighters still punch your flyers? If so, do you at least make them describe how they do it?</p>\n<p>Or do you just say, \"Flight has no inherent defensive benefit unless an Ability says so?\"</p>\n<p>&nbsp;</p>",
        "post_number": 1,
        "post_type": 1,
        "updated_at": "2021-02-07T01:53:53.417Z",
        "reply_count": 0,
        "reply_to_post_number": null,
        "quote_count": 0,
        "incoming_link_count": 3,
        "reads": 2,
        "readers_count": 1,
        "score": 15.4,
        "yours": false,
        "topic_id": 19981,
