      {
        "id": 231114,
        "name": "catDreaming",
        "username": "catDreaming",
        "avatar_template": "/letter_avatar_proxy/v4/letter/c/4491bb/{size}.png",
        "created_at": "2020-06-14T17:22:38.000Z",
        "cooked": "<p>I'd say that it's a narrative thing. If your flying thing is airborne, then it's probably safe from certain things.</p>\n<p>However, that doesn't mean that heroes should be locked out of interaction. Attacks can be emotional as well, or someone could take a Risky Action to hit a foe by doing something well, risky. Or, maybe a person uses a Hinder or Overcome to bring a flying character back to earth. Very much though, I see it as a narrative effect.</p>",
        "post_number": 2,
        "post_type": 1,
        "updated_at": "2021-02-07T06:06:17.343Z",
        "reply_count": 0,
        "reply_to_post_number": null,
