      {
        "id": 231118,
        "name": "Shadowstripe",
        "username": "Shadowstripe",
        "avatar_template": "/user_avatar/forums.greaterthangames.com/shadowstripe/{size}/1890_2.png",
        "created_at": "2020-06-18T19:49:22.000Z",
        "cooked": "<p>It really depends on how you decide to do things.</p>\n<p>Given the structure of the dice pools one makes (Power + Quality + Status), if one has the right powers, getting up close and personal with a flyer isn't that hard.&nbsp; Leaping is a great way to reach a flying target (it works for the Hulk at least), but Agility and even Speed have been used by various heroes and villains in comics to launch themselves into the air.&nbsp; Using the Acrobatics quality with a more offensive power could also work.<br>\n<br>\nAnd that isn't the end of the possibilities.&nbsp; Have a super strong character?&nbsp; Have them Boost your close combat character by throwing them at an airborne opponent... \"Fastball Special\" style!.<br>\n<br>\nIn short, the flexibility of the game design makes it easy to justify how almost any character can attack any opponent.&nbsp; All one really needs is a little creativity.</p>",
        "post_number": 6,
        "post_type": 1,
        "updated_at": "2021-02-07T06:06:17.646Z",
        "reply_count": 0,
        "reply_to_post_number": null,
        "quote_count": 0,
        "incoming_link_count": 0,
        "reads": 1,
        "readers_count": 0,
        "score": 0.2,
        "yours": false,
        "topic_id": 19981,
        "topic_slug": "flight",
