        "can_see_hidden_post": false,
        "can_wiki": false,
        "read": false,
        "user_title": null,
        "bookmarked": false,
        "raw": "<p>It really depends on how you decide to do things.</p>\r\n\r\n<p>Given the structure of the dice pools one makes (Power + Quality + Status), if one has the right powers, getting up close and personal with a flyer isn't that hard.&nbsp; Leaping is a great way to reach a flying target (it works for the Hulk at least), but Agility and even Speed have been used by various heroes and villains in comics to launch themselves into the air.&nbsp; Using the Acrobatics quality with a more offensive power could also work.<br />\r\n<br />\r\nAnd that isn't the end of the possibilities.&nbsp; Have a super strong character?&nbsp; Have them Boost your close combat character by throwing them at an airborne opponent... \"Fastball Special\" style!.<br />\r\n<br />\r\nIn short, the flexibility of the game design makes it easy to justify how almost any character can attack any opponent.&nbsp; All one really needs is a little creativity.</p>",
