      {
        "id": 231119,
        "name": "Cult of Gloom",
        "username": "Cult_of_Gloom",
        "avatar_template": "/user_avatar/forums.greaterthangames.com/cult_of_gloom/{size}/1878_2.png",
        "created_at": "2020-06-18T21:00:00.000Z",
        "cooked": "<p>its really hard for me to think of a situation in which merely being airborne would make it impossible for a player to affect the target in some fashion.</p>\n<p>I could see them being unaffected by certain actions, like if the player has an ability that makes the ground a swirling whirlpool of sand for a large group hinder that might not work on&nbsp; a group of flying enemies.</p>\n<p>I could see the flying enemies having an advantage. You decide to give them a plus 1 bonus on minion saves against attacks coming at them from the ground because they are really good and mobile flyers.</p>\n<p>But i can't&nbsp; think of a situation in which the character wouldn 't be able to make some kind of attack.</p>",
        "post_number": 7,
